     function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint value) returns (bool success) {
         if (frozenAccount[msg.sender]) return false;
         if(balances[from] < value) return false;
         if( allowed[from][msg.sender] >= value ) return false;
         if(balances[to] + value < balances[to]) return false;
         balances[from] -= value;
         allowed[from][msg.sender] -= value;
         balances[to] += value;
         Transfer(from, to, value);
         return true;
     }
     ```
   - Vulnerability: The code does not correctly handle the logic for transferring tokens from one address to another. It does not check if the `value` parameter is greater than the current allowance for the sender.
   - Reason: The code does not check if the `value` parameter is greater than the current allowance for the sender. This can lead to incorrect token transfers and potential loss of tokens.

